<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 8 February, from 1238 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-horde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1238 <span class="tih-ago">788 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols sack Vladimir in north-eastern Rus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Batu Khan's army stormed and burned Vladimir, the capital of the leading Russian principality. The Mongol conquest brought the Russian lands under the Golden Horde for some two centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-armada.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1587 <span class="tih-ago">439 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is executed at Fotheringhay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After nineteen years in English captivity, Mary was beheaded for plotting against Elizabeth I. Her execution removed the Catholic claimant to the English throne and helped provoke the Spanish Armada.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1693 <span class="tih-ago">333 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal charter founds the College of William and Mary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William III and Mary II granted a charter for a college in Virginia, later sited at Williamsburg. It is the second-oldest college in the United States; Thomas Jefferson studied there.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delaware rejects the Thirteenth Amendment</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delaware's legislature voted against the amendment abolishing slavery, although the state had remained in the Union. It ratified the amendment only symbolically, in 1901.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1904 <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks the Russian fleet at Port Arthur</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese torpedo boats struck the Russian Pacific squadron at night, opening the Russo-Japanese War. Japan's victory in 1905 was the first by an Asian power over a European one in modern times.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'The Birth of a Nation' premieres in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">D. W. Griffith's Civil War epic pioneered techniques of film storytelling but glorified the Ku Klux Klan. It drew protests from the NAACP and helped inspire the Klan's revival that year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1974 <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skylab 4 crew return after 84 days in space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Carr, Edward Gibson and William Pogue splashed down after the longest crewed mission yet. Their experience of long-duration flight informed later space stations.</p></div></li></ol>
